# CORS headers for API access.
#
# Keep comments OUTSIDE the rule blocks. Cloudflare Pages parses every
# indented line under a path as `name: value`, so an indented `#` comment
# is an invalid line — and the first version of the Link rule below sat
# after such a comment and was silently dropped for a full deploy cycle
# while CORS above it kept working.
#
# RFC 9727 catalog advertisement: this host is the likeliest place an
# agent enters the project — it is the API — and www alone used to send
# the header, so an agent that landed on /v1/ had no path to the catalog,
# the auth policy or the MCP server. The URL is absolute, unlike www's
# copy: the catalog document is centralised on www so there is one copy
# that cannot drift, and a relative `/.well-known/api-catalog` here would
# resolve against this host, where it 404s. The catalog sends
# `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, so cross-origin agents can follow it.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, HEAD, OPTIONS
  Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
  Link: <https://www.wheelofheaven.world/.well-known/api-catalog>; rel="api-catalog"

# Cache control for API responses
/v1/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
